From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Desidero <desidero@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 16:08:59 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(web): record comments on stored open items as their
 answers

Answering several items at once sends one "Comments on N items" message,
which tells the agent but leaves every stored item open in the panel until
the agent gets round to closing it, so the panel cannot tell what still
waits on the user.

When that message posts (the moment its drafts are settled), the browser
that sent it records each item's comments as the item's answer through
POST /v1/sessions/{id}/open-items/answers: an open stored item becomes
answered, shows the answer, and leaves the badge. The message goes through
the normal send path first and nothing waits on the record: on a server
without open items nothing is sent, and a refused or failed call only
leaves the items open. An expanded row in the panel also offers Comment.

"Comment and close", chosen per item in comment mode (the comment's header
card, the tray's toggle, or an expanded panel row), settles an item with
the comment itself. The item's heading in the message ends "(closed by me)",
so the agent knows, and once the message posts the item is also closed
through PATCH /v1/sessions/{id}/open-items as the user, the comment its
resolution. It is offered only on stored items that are not closed; a close
that fails leaves the item open with its answer and says so in a toast.

Not proposed upstream yet: the comments and the store it joins are not
upstream either.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: Desidero <desidero@gmail.com>
